course: dictionary
lesson: 14146
title: Misfortune and bad luck
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Misfortune means bad luck. A misfortune is one unlucky event that happens to someone. When you meet this word, ask: did something bad happen that was not the person's fault? If yes, it is probably a misfortune.
explain: «Sam had the misfortune to break his arm on the first day of his holiday.» Had the misfortune to means it was unlucky for Sam. He did not plan it. The clue is that something bad happened to him on the first day, so misfortune is bad luck.
explain: «The village suffered a series of misfortunes: a flood, then a fire, then a long drought.» A series of misfortunes means many bad events, one after another. In stories, characters often suffer misfortune, and then things get better. Look for that change to help you understand the word.
fact: Misfortune means bad luck.
fact: A misfortune is an unlucky event that happens to someone.
fact: You can say «a misfortune» for one event, or just «misfortune» for bad luck in general.
fact: Useful phrases: «have the misfortune to», «suffer misfortune», and «a series of misfortunes».
fact: Misfortune is about things that happen to you, not things you choose to do.
exercise: «The little dog had the misfortune to fall into the pond.» What does misfortune mean here? | *Bad luck | A long swim | A special treat | A new game
exercise: What does «a series of misfortunes» mean? | A set of new tools | A long, quiet walk | *Many bad events, one after another | One happy surprise
exercise: Which word means bad luck? | reward | treat | *misfortune | prize
test: «Mia had the misfortune to lose her purse on the bus.» What was Mia's misfortune? | Catching the bus | Buying a ticket | *Losing her purse | Finding a coin
test: Which phrase means to go through bad luck? | *suffer misfortune | win a prize | make a wish | have a party
exam: «Ali's bike got a puncture on the way to school, which was a small misfortune.» Why is this a misfortune? | He chose to ride too fast on purpose | *It was bad luck that happened to him | It made him late for a party | It was a lucky win
